;; The datetime differential corpus: every KNOWN divergence from a real
;; PostgreSQL, one entry per sample. Generated by
;;   (datahike.fuzz.differential/run-surface :datetime 0 0)
;;
;; A divergence NOT listed here fails `bb fuzz datetime`. A listed
;; one that now agrees also fails, with BASELINE DRIFT -- so a fix
;; is not complete until its entries are pruned from this file.
;;
;; WAS 239 of 670 before the ParseDateTime/DecodeDateTime port.
;; Every one that is left is the SAME deferral:
;;
;;   DEFERRED -- `now`, `today`, `tomorrow`, `yesterday`. The parser
;;     reads them correctly; `cast.clj/datetime-ctx` withholds the
;;     clock on purpose, because a cast is constant-folded into a
;;     cached plan and a folded `'today'::date` would freeze there.
;;
;; The 2 CARRIER entries that were here are GONE: a timestamptz now
;; uses an OffsetDateTime, which keeps microseconds AND renders the
;; `+00` that a java.util.Date was being used for.
;;
;; NOTE what this corpus does NOT see. Every sample is
;; `SELECT '<lit>'::<type>::text`, so it cannot tell a parser loss
;; from a renderer loss, and it never exercises a column, an array,
;; COPY, a set operation or a comparison. Three real divergences
;; lived in those paths while this file read 25.
;;
;; WHICH PostgreSQL: generated against the local oracle, 17.10, while
;; CI pins cimg/postgres:17.7. CI has run this manifest against 17.7
;; with neither an unexpected divergence nor a drift, so the two
;; releases agree on all 670 samples.
;;
;; Baseline 2026-10-03: 23 of 670 samples diverge.

[{:surface :datetime,
  :key "SELECT 'now'::date::text",
  :reason
  "DEFERRED: a clock-reading token. The parser handles these -- pass a `:now` and they work -- but `cast.clj/datetime-ctx` supplies none on purpose, because a cast is constant-folded into a cached plan and folding `today` once would freeze it for that plan's life. Needs the deferred treatment `now()` gets."}
